# Generated catalogue artifacts — never hand-merge these.
#
# catalogue.json, index-fragment.json and artifacts/*.json are produced
# deterministically by scripts/build_fragment.py + scripts/merge_catalog.py (the
# "Build catalogue" CI workflow) from apps/<id>/manifest.json + curation.json +
# sources.json. They MUST be committed (served raw via GitHub Pages /
# raw.githubusercontent.com), so they can't be .gitignored — but a hand-merge of
# their conflict markers is never correct.
#
# The "ours" merge driver auto-resolves any merge/rebase conflict in these files
# to the current side (no conflict markers); CI then regenerates the
# authoritative content on the next apps/ or curation.json push. If you need the
# local copy exact after an auto-resolved merge, just run:
#     make catalog        # = build_fragment.py --source base + merge_catalog.py
#
# REQUIRES a one-time, per-clone config — the driver command lives in
# .git/config, which git does NOT track:
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
# Without it, git falls back to a normal text merge and the conflicts return.
catalogue.json      merge=ours linguist-generated=true
index-fragment.json merge=ours linguist-generated=true
artifacts/*.json    merge=ours linguist-generated=true
